troduced to in the entire  series followed soon after by sengoku's  golden buddha fruit and now we're not  counting the nika fruit since it wasn't  formally introduced until very recently  so why exactly is marco so loved by us  fans sure he has an awesome power but  that alone can't justify his wild wild  popularity among a cast with so many  fantastically written characters i mean  not only does he outrank whitebeard  among the fanbase but heavy hitters like  blackbeard garp and even doflamingo it's  not just the powers of the phoenix but  the meaning behind the phoenix as a  animal and how marco embodies that  meaning that delivers his characters to  such extreme heights  the heights of popularity not the kind  of heights he achieves by flying i guess  that's obvious so yeah someday in the  final saga we may get to see marco die  and resurrect literally as many predict  the phoenix fruit will allow him to do  however i want to theorize that in a way  marco has already died and resurrected  and in doing so has shown what it really  takes to be the first mate of an emperor  of the sea also quick shout out to  patricia and austin singer both of whom  are subscribed to the channel and thus  have helped us increase our bouncy by  100 barries each advancing us on our  shared mission to overtake trebled  bounty and reach 100 million berries so  zorro rayleigh katakuri marco so often  in one piece the first mates are the  coolest characters on their cruise and  in the story overall if we're being  honest many fans included would rank  zorro as their favorite straw hat over  luffy due to his epic three sword style  feats rayleigh stopped an admiral slight  speed kick with a sandal katakuri's  design initially looked so edgy that he  seemed to be out of place in one piece  but quickly became a beloved antagonist  and when i say that these characters are  cool i don't just mean they're awesome  which they are these characters all have  subdued personalities partnered with  effortless feats of brutal strength all  of them are laid back in the face of  immense danger and they just ooze  coolness but is that what really makes a  great first mate  no it takes a lot more than being cool  to be the first mate to the world's  greatest pirates each of these pirates  carries the burden when their captain no  longer can in other words when the  number one is absent or incapacitated  they are the leaders to their crews they  inherit the will of their captains when  luffy was unconscious on thriller bark  zoro took on his pain in order to save  the crew and he did so unselfishly  proclaiming that nothing happened after  roger's execution rayleigh waited  decades on saba odi until he found his  captain's successor he trained luffy so  that he would stand a chance on the  journey ahead in a new world and  eventually could find love tale during  big mom's hunger pains when she destroys  her own island and even devours her own  children it's katakuri who protects his  family members at all costs and so of  course marco also carries on the will of  whitebeards and in doing so he embodies  the spirit of his devil fruit the  phoenix in the legend of the phoenix  this fiery bird makes its nest and then  dies engulfed in flames from the ashes  that remain it is reborn as an egg  hatching again into a new phoenix which  is also why we have to ask ourselves at  this point in the story whether baron  tamago has a technically more accurate  phoenix fruit than marco does on a more  serious note though it's fitting that  this story would fit so neatly into  mythology after all we do know that oda  loves drawing on various myths and  legends from all around the world the  journey of the phoenix can be found in  legends from all types of countries and  places the journey of marco actually  parallels a literal concept called the  monomyth the scholar joseph campbell in  his book the hero with a thousand faces  recognized that many myths and legends  from across the world do share similar  structures this shared common structure  for stories is called the monomyth or  the hero's journey one focal part of the  hero's journey comes after a great  challenge they fall into an abyss an  absolute low point a death and a rebirth  ultimately after their rebirth they rise  into overcoming their challenges and  finding atonement and so of course the  entirety of luffy's story for instance  mirrors the hero's journey very well as  well his lowest point was losing his  brother at marine ford a period of utter  despair and hopelessness that he was  then reborn from after the time skip but  we also see this concept represented in  miniature with marco and the legend of  the phoenix in general after the war at  marineford when the white pit pirates  lost both their captain and ace marco  stepped up to the role of leader as a  new captain he sought vengeance against  blackbeard the traitor who had caused  unspeakable damage to his former crew  however in this payback war the remnants  of the whitebeard pirates suffered a  devastating loss and subsequently had to  disband and so if marco's journey  parallels the mythology of the phoenix  then this is his death well once he  soared into battle he went out in a  blaze of glory seemingly completely  defeated it was then that he retreated  to things island even after the end of  his crew he never lost sight of  fulfilling his captain's will marco  protected the island that whitebeard  considered his treasure using his  medical knowledge to take care of the  people there and watching over the  graves of ace and his captain even  though his personal battle had ended  embers remained in the ashes still  burning softly with the dreams of the  late edward new gates and so it was of  course in wano that the phoenix would  rise once again reunited with another  former division commander izo marco  returned to the battlefields after  hearing nekomamushi's plea for help he  knew it's what whitebeard would have  done to help avenge his old friend  kozuki odin now with stylish new glasses  which you know we could see as a new  clarity of vision at the risk of maybe  overanalyzing this a little bit you know  let's do it anyways marco's phoenix form  burned again clashing with some of the  great powers of the world the commanders  of two yonko crews and briefly with big  mom herself his healing powers came in  clutch during the battle and he even  helped zorro make it in time to  participate in roof piece many fans also  see marco as the pheasant parallel  within the momotaro myth in which  momonosuke restored his kingdom with the  help of a monkey luffy a dog yamato and  the pheasant which is marco the phoenix  played an invaluable role in the ninja  pirate mink samurai alliance and likely  helped turn the tide of the battle for  wano country now it's still unknown to  us what will actually become of marco in  the final saga but surely there is more  to his story as far as we know  whitebeard's supposed sun weevil is  still hunting the remnants of the wiper  pirates will he eventually restore this  crew to the form of glory finally making  a true rebirth will the rest of the  division commanders that we haven't seen  post timeskip make an appearance maybe  there's still hope too that the  figurative death and rebirth that marco  has followed in the story so far will be  followed by a literal death  and rebirth enabled by his mythical zone  fruit and who knows maybe he will even  sail with the straw hats for a little  bit in a recent video on this channel  the phoenix fruit was actually named the  most powerful of all the zone devil  fruits and if you want to know the  secret to why it is the best of the best  and see what fruit it narrowly beat you  really should miss out on that video  right here

